    "narrative": "A 69-year-old woman with metastatic non-small-cell lung cancer and hospice status, who recently required drainage for a malignant pericardial effusion, presented with new aphasia and right facial droop. Evaluation revealed a cerebrovascular accident and a transient inferior myocardial infarction. Her ECG showed normalization of prior ST elevations with Q waves and first-degree AV block, and labs showed a leukopenia of 1.3 and hematocrit of 31. The case was discussed with the patient and her daughter, who understood the guarded prognosis. Heparin continuation was deemed reasonable with acknowledgment of hemorrhagic effusion risk, morphine was advised for comfort and preload reduction, and other blood thinners like Plavix or thrombolytics were avoided. She is being admitted by the hospitalist service.",
